        "Integrate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 6(3x - 5)^3 - \\frac{3}{2}x^2$ with respect to $x$ using the reverse chain rule:\n$$y = \\int \\left[6(3x - 5)^3 - \\frac{3}{2}x^2\\right] dx = \\frac{6(3x - 5)^4}{4 \\times 3} - \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right) + c = \\frac{1}{2}(3x - 5)^4 - \\frac{1}{2}x^3 + c$$",
        "Substitute the coordinates $(2, -3.5)$ to find $c$:\n$$-3.5 = \\frac{1}{2}(3(2) - 5)^4 - \\frac{1}{2}(2^3) + c = \\frac{1}{2}(1)^4 - \\frac{1}{2}(8) + c = 0.5 - 4 + c = -3.5 + c$$",
        "Solve for $c$:\n$$c = 0$$",
        "State the equation of the curve:\n$$y = \\frac{1}{2}(3x - 5)^4 - \\frac{1}{2}x^3$$"
